Multiply numbers, not strings.

The Math tamper plugin multiplied its two operands raw. Everything that reaches
it from an entity field arrives as a string, and PHP's loose typing then decides
what the result should be on its own. With decimal values written in the
database as '12.50' that guesswork is wrong often enough to matter: the ERP uses
this plugin through eca_tamper to work out line totals, so a bad multiplication
lands straight in a sales order.

The other three operations are left alone on purpose. Only multiplication was
producing wrong figures on this site, and a wider change would be a bigger bet
than the evidence supports.

This fix was applied by hand to the module folder at some point before August
2026 and was found again while reconciling the site with Composer. It lives here
now so that reinstalling the module cannot silently undo it.

diff --git a/src/Plugin/Tamper/Math.php b/src/Plugin/Tamper/Math.php
--- a/src/Plugin/Tamper/Math.php
+++ b/src/Plugin/Tamper/Math.php
@@ -153,7 +153,7 @@ class Math extends TamperBase {
         break;
 
       case 'multiplication':
-        $data = $data * $value;
+        $data = (float) $data * (float) $value;
         break;
 
       case 'division':
